// =============================================
// Detection: Password Spray Attack
// Author: Eros Marin Morales
// Data Source: Microsoft Entra ID Sign-in Logs
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.003 - Password Spraying
// Severity: High
//
// Purpose:
// Detect a single IP address attempting
// authentication against multiple accounts.
//
// Why it matters:
// Password spraying is commonly used by
// attackers to gain initial access while
// avoiding account lockouts.
//
// Investigation Steps:
// 1. Review source IP address.
// 2. Count affected users.
// 3. Check geolocation.
// 4. Review sign-in history.
// 5. Determine if MFA blocked the attempts.
//
// Potential False Positives:
// - Internal vulnerability scanners.
// - Penetration testing activities.
// - Authentication misconfigurations.
//
// Recommended Response:
// - Block malicious IP.
// - Investigate impacted accounts.
// - Verify MFA enforcement.
// - Reset compromised credentials if needed.
// =============================================

SigninLogs
| where ResultType != 0
| summarize
    FailedAttempts = count(),
    TargetedUsers = dcount(UserPrincipalName)
by IPAddress
| where FailedAttempts > 20
| where TargetedUsers > 5
| sort by FailedAttempts desc
